a discovery as beautiful as it is  hopeful  this huge reef filled with rose-shaped  corals was found by scientists off the  coast of tahiti  unusually it's in pristine condition  unharmed by pollution or people  well it's exciting because it's uh it's  a healthy reef and  you know  if you look at the stories it's it's  quite  quite going the opposite we have lost  about half of our coral reefs in the  last 70 years  and uh it's really the stuff that makes  you dream and it makes you really  understand the beauty and the treasure  of the uh of a marine environment in the  ocean  the reef was discovered by a team of  unesco scientists using state-of-the-art  diving equipment that allowed them to  stay deeper  after 200 hours of diving they measured  the reef at three kilometers long and  stretching down to 70 meters below sea  level that makes it one of the world's  largest at this depth and raises the  prospect of more reefs waiting to be  found  more dives are planned in the coming  months to study the reef and the marine  life that has made it their home  but its discovery shows how little we  still know about our underwater world  katie barnfield sky news
 

